# Java Interview Refresh

Reference: `content/java-engineering/top-100-java-interview-questions.md`, `content/java-engineering/language-fundamentals.md`

## Audience

Experienced Java engineers, leads, and architects who need a fast interview refresh. Not a beginner tutorial and not an internals curriculum.

## Primary Course

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `data/java_engineering_modules.yaml` | 6 modules, one cheat sheet each |
| `data/java_engineering_order.yaml` | Flat previous/next navigation |
| `scripts/build_java_engineering_handbook.py` | Sync course order; preserve optional depth pages |
| `content/java-engineering/<slug>.md` | Hand-maintained refresh sheets and optional references |

URL: `/java-engineering/<slug>/` - use `aliases:` in front matter for renamed slugs.

## Page Format (`cheatSheet: true`)

1. At a Glance - 2-3 bullets
2. Decision/reference tables
3. Production scenarios or answer frame
4. Quick Gotchas
5. See Also

Answers should lead with the decision, constraint, and trade-off. Explain internals only in direct response to an explicit interviewer probe.

## Modules

1. Core Java Refresh
2. Collections Refresh
3. Concurrency Refresh
4. JVM in Production
5. Modern Java
6. Interview Sprint

Each module contains one compact cheat sheet. Deep internals pages may remain as optional references but must not appear in the primary course unless specifically requested.

## Out of Scope

Spring Boot, Hibernate, build tools, design patterns, DSA, and distributed-system design belong in their dedicated sections.

## Maintenance

```bash
python scripts/build_java_engineering_handbook.py
```

Page bodies are hand-maintained. The build script synchronizes navigation and does not delete unlisted depth pages.
